, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/A3_Yanling_2.png?resize=768%2C177&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/A3_Yanling_2.png?resize=1200%2C277&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/A3_Yanling_2.png?w=1415&amp;ssl=1 1415w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\">.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rectification<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">With the warping function implemented, I first it on a single image. I selected a <strong>floor pattern<\/strong> from the game, as the texture and perspective details make it an ideal example for homography-based warping. To prepare the image, I cropped a portion of the scene to focus on the floor region and reduce unnecessary computation from surrounding objects. Then, I applied <strong>bilinear interpolation<\/strong> using the implemented <code><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);color:#cf2e2e\" class=\"has-inline-color\">warpImageBilinear()<\/mark><\/code> function to perform the perspective transformation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"375\" data-attachment-id=\"890\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/?attachment_id=890\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/yanling_floor.jpg?fit=600%2C375&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"600,375\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0